  "label": "intended audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed for an audience that may be receptive to or familiar with anti-Asian racist stereotypes, particularly those targeting Chinese people. The use of Prince Charles and Camilla, Duchess of Cornwall, as visual anchors implies the target audience is likely Western, particularly British, viewers who associate the royal family with moral authority and Western civility. The meme leverages this association to frame the offensive text as a 'fact' or 'shock' that the royal couple would supposedly find repulsive, thereby appealing to an audience that identifies with or admires the monarchy and its perceived cultural superiority. The target audience is likely to be individuals who hold or are exposed to anti-Asian sentiment, and who may find the juxtaposition of the royal couple with the racist text humorous or provocative, even if it is hateful. The meme's effectiveness relies on the audience's acceptance of the false stereotype about Chinese people eating dogs and their willingness to engage with the derogatory labels 'savages' and 'disgusting' as part of a broader anti-Asian narrative.",
